  "regressions": [
    "three bursts of ASCII, punctuation, Chinese and emoji; immediate following Return observes the text",
    "16 select-all/replace cycles and explicit restoration, retaining original fixture process and contents",
    "End at current boundary, Left and Backspace immediately followed by text",
    "1.25-second client stall before delivery: bounded refusal, no insertion",
    "1.25-second client stall after editing but before acknowledgement: uncertain outcome, later text rejected, no replay; late acknowledgement and explicit restore recover",
    "actual GNOME private extension disable/enable restores and reinstalls observers; original application remains alive",
    "native PNG 2940x1604 and 2940x1846, 1x/2x viewports, H264 960x540",
    "shared Xwayland high-DPI migration refuses before mutation; raw capture 2940x1660/2800x1500 and scoped pointer mapping remain correct"
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "The single-line GTK fixture sends no input-state acknowledgement after Return. Following text is refused before editing until a new state is confirmed (e.g. Ctrl+A/refocus); explicit whole-text paste remains a separate operation. This is a validated capability boundary, not unconditional support for every control.",
    "Real Firefox after activation, real IME candidate composition, real desktop Portal authorization and physical multi-device simultaneous input are not accepted by these fixture tests.",
    "No full bidirectional physical-device E2E or CI this turn."
  ],
  "gates": {
    "mac_check_sh": "passed: 49 Rust passed / 5 ignored; 24 frontend tests; JS completion/acknowledgement unit cases; Swift/AppKit scoped errors and reconnect; two actual isolated QUIC nodes with video and binary transfer",
